WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
Stannis Baratheon: My brother, Robert Baratheon,&nbsp;
had raised the banners of Storm's End, our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:12.880
ancestral castle, against the Mad King Aerys.
Jon Arryn of the Vale and Eddard Stark of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:18.080
the North stood with him, and Hoster&nbsp;
Tully of the Riverlands would join.
&nbsp;

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:23.720
But their lands were far from ours and&nbsp;
separated by the combined strength of the West,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:30.120
the Reach, and King's Landing itself. Even&nbsp;
Robert's own lords were against him.
&nbsp;

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:37.480
It was the hardest choice I've ever made: my&nbsp;
brother or my king, blood or honor. Aerys ruled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:45.120
by right of all the laws in Westeros. Everyone&nbsp;
knew the price of defiance. But there are deeper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.120 --> 00:01:08.200
older laws: the younger brother bows&nbsp;
before the elder. I followed Robert.
&nbsp;

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:13.680
Early in the war, Mace Tyrell's indecisive&nbsp;
victory at Ashford cut Robert off from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:20.320
Storm's End. Instead of pursuing Robert,&nbsp;
and risking his record, Mace Tyrell turned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:26.280
east and laid siege to our home.
His vast army and navy encircled us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:32.520
and preventing any resupply by land or sea.&nbsp;
If a wagon tried to reach us, it was burned.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:38.040
If a ship tried to land, it was sunk.
We were locked inside Storm's End to starve.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:43.560
But Robert had commanded me to hold the castle&nbsp;
no matter the cost. He could ill afford to lose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:50.560
his ancient seat, which had never fallen.
While Robert smashed Rhaegar on the Trident,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:57.600
my men ate the dogs because the horses had&nbsp;
already been devoured. While the Lannisters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:03.600
sacked King's Landing, we ate the rats.
If the smuggler Davos had not slipped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:09.480
through the Tyrell blockade with his&nbsp;
onions, we'd have eaten our own dead.
&nbsp;

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:17.600
But I held the castle until Lord Eddard remembered&nbsp;
us, and marched to lift the siege. The Tyrells&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:25.880
didn't even put up a fight, and Robert threw a&nbsp;
feast to celebrate Lord Eddard's "victory."
&nbsp;

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:31.760
I was sent to the royal island stronghold of&nbsp;
Dragonstone to deal with Viserys and Daenerys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:37.360
the last surviving Targaryen children.
Before I arrived, however, they had escaped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:45.480
across the Narrow Sea. Robert was furious.&nbsp;
He stripped me of Storm's End and gave it to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:53.040
that prancing fool Renly, my younger brother.
Davos Seaworth: Wars are not as good for smugglers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:59.880
as you'd think. Every harbor fills with guards and&nbsp;
inspectors, and the seas fill with blockades and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:05.600
pirates paid by each side to prey on the other.
Though I had no love for the Mad King, I'd grown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:11.560
up around the power of King's Landing. I figured&nbsp;
this Robert Baratheon would end as the other rebel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:17.960
lords: burned to ash. But he didn't. 
The North, the Riverlands, and the Vale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:23.720
joined him. And in the taverns, people&nbsp;
drank to Robert's health openly. "Brave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:29.120
fools," I thought. But I had a family who'd&nbsp;
be left in the cold if I lost my head.
&nbsp;

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:35.000
When Mace Tyrell marched on Robert's home at&nbsp;
Storm's End, I spied the end of the rebellion.
&nbsp;

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:39.440
The castle was garrisoned by Robert's&nbsp;
younger brother Stannis and a small guard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:45.240
and would not hold out for long. When it fell,&nbsp;
Robert would be homeless, and his support would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:51.680
bleed away. This, I knew from experience.
Months later, Stannis was still holding the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:59.960
castle. Nobody cared. But on voyages, I had seen&nbsp;
what famine does; and I thought of all those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:08.040
men in Storm's End, who would die unmourned and&nbsp;
forgotten. No better than Flea Bottom orphans.
&nbsp;

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:15.040
I told his wife, and myself, that I'd get a high&nbsp;
price for the onions and salt beef. In truth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:20.000
I knew I'd be captured by the Tyrell galleys&nbsp;
or drowned. But I was too stubborn.
&nbsp;

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:25.640
Later that night, in the dark, in a tiny boat&nbsp;
with a black sail, I cursed myself and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:32.400
moonlight as I waited for the tide to turn.
When it did, the wind beat the sail so hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:39.160
I ripped it down, fearing the Tyrell ships&nbsp;
would hear. Luckily, they had grown lax.
&nbsp;

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:45.080
With muffled oars, alone, I steered my cargo&nbsp;
through the treacherous currents and snarls of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:51.560
rock that gave Shipbreaker Bay its name.
The waves finally carried me, soaked and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:57.160
near-blind from seawater, through the&nbsp;
mouth of the cavern beneath the castle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:02.520
Then Stannis Baratheon arrived.
The siege had left him gaunt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:08.840
but not weak, never weak. He greeted me&nbsp;
and accepted my onions with cool courtesy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:16.400
betraying no emotion even as all wept.
He doled out the food to his wife and each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:24.120
of his men before he ate himself, a portion no&nbsp;
larger than any other. When he finally thanked me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:29.960
I could see his mind had already returned&nbsp;
to the castle's defense. His duty.
&nbsp;

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:35.960
After Aerys fell and Lord Stark lifted&nbsp;
the siege, Stannis summoned me. For my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:42.160
salvation of Storm's End, I was to be granted&nbsp;
a knighthood, a keep of my own, and my son&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:48.280
taken into Stannis's personal service.
"Davos of Flea Bottom" had become "Ser&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:53.800
Davos of House Seaworth," and my son&nbsp;
would serve the king's own brother.
&nbsp;

00:05:53.800 --> 00:06:00.120
But for my previous crimes as a smuggler, I&nbsp;
was to have the fingertips of one hand taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:05.760
off above the highest joint. Stannis held that&nbsp;
I had flouted the laws of the land for years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:13.120
and a good act does not wash out the bad.
In one fell swoop, or five, Stannis gave my son&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:19.480
a future and my family a name that I could've&nbsp;
never imagined, nor earned, on my own.
&nbsp;

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:24.440
I still keep the finger bones in a bag&nbsp;
around my neck to remind me of what I was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:29.640
and what I owe to Stannis.
For during my many years as a smuggler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:35.960
I visited many ports, taverns, and back&nbsp;
alleys, and saw many things in this world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:45.240
but never justice. Until Stannis.
Robert Baratheon: Rebellion! The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:54.080
crimes of House Targaryen were too heinous to go&nbsp;
unanswered. The noble Houses of Baratheon, Stark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.080 --> 00:07:01.080
and Arryn, united to oppose and overthrow&nbsp;
the line of the cursed dragon kings.
&nbsp;

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:06.840
While Ned Stark and Arryn secured an&nbsp;
alliance with the Tullys of Riverrun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:12.520
I called the banners of Storm's End and&nbsp;
rode out in force against the Mad King and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:20.800
his minions. Gods, those were some battles!
Our first victory occurred at Summerhall where I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:27.560
faced off against an army of dragon loyalists and&nbsp;
won three battles in a single day, three in one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:34.840
day! Seven hells, that was a glorious day!
We tried to take Ashford Castle in the Reach,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:43.440
but the Tyrells beat us back. We had to regroup.&nbsp;
My army was pursued north by Aerys's army and took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:49.640
refuge in the Stoney Sept in the Riverlands.
When the Targaryen army entered the town,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:54.360
the sept bells tolled, a signal to the&nbsp;
townspeople of the battle that was to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.360 --> 00:08:01.680
come. As the Targaryens searched from house to&nbsp;
house for me, the combined forces of Ned Stark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:08.480
and the Tullys swept into the city.
Gods, what a day that was! It's now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:15.040
known as the Battle of the Bells. We&nbsp;
overwhelmed the Mad King's forces and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:23.080
sent them scampering back to King's Landing.
Aerys's son, Rhaegar, who started the whole damn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:30.120
thing, finally emerged from hiding in the South&nbsp;
and assembled his own army to face us. As for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:36.840
Mad King, he must have been pissing himself.
The battle that would decide the fate of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:42.960
Seven Kingdoms occurred at the crossing&nbsp;
of the Green Fork of the Trident river.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:48.280
Rhaegar commanded the royal host, which&nbsp;
was some forty thousand strong.
&nbsp;

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:56.720
My forces were outnumbered by nearly five thousand&nbsp;
men, but that didn't matter. They were fresh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:02.240
but we were battle-hardened&nbsp;
and had justice on our side.
&nbsp;

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:08.880
As the battle raged around us, I faced off&nbsp;
with Rhaegar. The stag and the dragon right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:14.160
there in the ford of the river. I&nbsp;
fought with the fury of ten men,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:21.520
raining blow after blow upon that vile prince&nbsp;
before burying my war hammer in his chest.
&nbsp;

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:25.560
I hit him so hard, the rubies on his&nbsp;
armor broke free, flinging them into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:33.440
the stream. They call it the Ruby Ford now.
With that scum Rhaegar dead and the royal army&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:40.600
shattered, our next move was to make for King's&nbsp;
Landing. But I'd sustained a few wounds in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:46.520
battle and was unable to ride. I sent Ned&nbsp;
Stark to the capital to face the Mad King&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:52.680
and make him pay for his crimes.
Viserys Targaryen: The Targaryens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:57.600
blood of the dragon and the last of Old&nbsp;
Valyria, were loved by their subjects and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:03.320
admired far and wide as the greatest dynasty&nbsp;
in the history of the western world.
&nbsp;

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:07.960
But the peace and prosperity of nearly&nbsp;
three centuries of Targaryen rule&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:14.480
were shattered by the Usurper, Robert&nbsp;
Baratheon, and his band of traitors.
&nbsp;

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:20.640
House Baratheon owed its very existence to&nbsp;
the Targaryens. Was it not Aegon the Dragon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:25.720
himself, who elevated the bastard Orys&nbsp;
Baratheon in the War of Conquest?
&nbsp;

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:31.120
And what of the Starks? The&nbsp;
Lannisters? The Arryns of the Vale?
&nbsp;

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:36.320
All had been spared and allowed to keep their&nbsp;
lands when Aegon could easily have wiped them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:45.160
out. Centuries later, the Usurper and his lackeys&nbsp;
repaid Aegon's benevolence with treachery.
&nbsp;

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:51.440
There are some who dare to claim Robert and&nbsp;
his allies had reason to rebel. They say the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:58.800
crown prince stole the Usurper's lady love.
They say my father, King Aerys, murdered Rickard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:04.520
Stark and his son without just cause. Whether&nbsp;
these charges are true or not, it doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:10.840
matter! The dragon answers to no one.
Aerys's good name has been besmirched in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:17.120
the years since the rebellion. He has been&nbsp;
called a dangerous madman, a monster, a tyrant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:24.600
that brought his tragic end upon himself.
Lies! My father was a victim of weaklings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:29.040
in his council! Lackwits who&nbsp;
failed him in his hour of need,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:36.360
and let the rebellion spin out of control!
But it was not enough. The royal army was crushed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:42.360
at the Battle of the Trident. It was there the&nbsp;
valiant Rhaegar met Robert in single combat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:48.720
but the gods betrayed him, and he&nbsp;
perished by the Usurper's hand.
&nbsp;

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:55.360
As the Field of Fire had marked the end of the&nbsp;
Andals centuries before, the Battle of the Trident&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.360 --> 00:12:00.800
seemed to herald the end of the dragon kings.
When word reached the capital of my brother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:08.400
Rhaegar's death, my father Aerys moved to protect&nbsp;
me, as I was the surviving heir to the throne.
&nbsp;

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:13.400
He sent me to the island fortress of Dragonstone,&nbsp;
along with my mother, Queen Rhaella, who was great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:21.160
with child. But as my father, my king, Aerys&nbsp;
Targaryen, prepared to defend his throne to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:28.880
bitter end, little did he know of the horrors&nbsp;
and betrayals that awaited him and our family.

